    ​[head=3]On Pronouns[/head]


    This lesson will focus on pronouns. Pronouns are useful tools in language to shorten speech. However, they are a common place of confusion for grays: pronouns only work with shared understanding, and if the pronouns cannot be comprehended by their conversation partner, then they quickly become confusing.


    Understanding WHAT you're talking about can be a good north star for figuring out what your companions are trying to say. Even when you don't understand every bit and piece. Language learning is about filling those gaps!


    There is no better way in gray to channel that skill than pronouns. Much like Universal Common, maybe you can see the root words of gray pronouns.


    —


