    ​[head=3]Bonus conjugations![/head]


    Here are some fun bonus words! When conjugating words, grays have a few unique words more borrowed from their Universal Common counterparts! Consider this a more practical form of slang. If you want to sound truly fluent, try sprinkling these words into your speech!


    ​[bold]Mozz[/bold] - [italic]You're[/italic]


    ​[bold]Wezz[/bold] - [italic]We're[/italic]


    —


    ​[head=3]Culture Corner[/head]


    Pronouns in gray society are a bit of an oddity: more likely than not, the gray you speak to and interact with every day is a clone! Gray's primary form of reproduction is mixing genetic material and creating new grays in a lab. They lack the sexual dimorphism that resulted in the concept of gender as presented in other cultures.


    This is by no means universal for grays. Thousands of stars means thousands of possibilities! However, this means the type of gender associated with pronouns is a learned concept for a good portion of grays. 


    A typical gray will pick their pronouns after developing their “taste”, that is to say the pieces of media they have the most affinity for. This means that a grays pronouns are a choice of the gray themself and should be respected. It is an extension of their tastes, and they use it to further mimic their favorite characters or concepts from media.


    Here are some examples of grays adopting a wide spectrum of gender!


    There is a picture of a gray wearing baggy jeans and a t-shirt. They have a big black beanie with a human skull on it. HE HIM is written in big text.


    There is a picture of a gray wearing baggy jeans and a t-shirt. They have a big black beanie with a human skull on it. The only difference from the previous image is the gray has eye-liner. SHE HER is written in big text.


    There is a picture of a gray wearing baggy jeans and a t-shirt. They have a big black beaning with a human skull on it. The only difference from the previous two images is an inclusion of piercings. THEY THEM is written in big text.


    There is a picture with all three of the previous grays in it. It has large stylized text reading “The Three Broodges”. None of them are smiling.


